  "snapshot": {
    "code": "9896afa77453c6fc97b177e7cb0e65e6",
    "comment": "C190: adopted qualified FE5540-type compound reference, not a verified VRFB gasket grade or assay. Per 139 parts: 100 commercial FKM, 30 carbon black, 6 hydrated lime, 3 MgO and no ionic liquid. The commercial-FKM portion includes 1% generic incorporated cure allowance; modelled VDF/HFP/TFE polymer is 75/16/9 molar. Native ecoinvent 3.12 VDF replaces the local custom VDF route and retains its intrinsic burdens once. HFP/polymer and compound stages are expanded into this existing gasket record. Qualified 95% retention, utilities and complete collection of nominal 0.04917459346181717 kg manufacturing loss to generic hazardous-waste incineration are engineering assumptions. Collection mass-routing alternatives are 0/50/100%; uncollected species and actual fluorinated destruction remain unresolved, not zero emissions or environmental bounds. Patent US20130109790A1 supports formulation context; cure chemistry, industrial energy, actual grade and treatment adequacy remain unverified. Existing gasket quantities, freight and stack-owned retirement are preserved; no additional whole-gasket disposal or recovery credit.\n\nHistorical source/curation record:\nFKM gaskets represent the first modeled variant. An important type of FKM is the terpolymer consisting of vinylidene fluoride (VDF), hexafluoropropylene (HFP) and tetrafluoroethylene (TFE). The respective ecoinvent datasets of the chemicals are used in which HFE is approximated by HFP and VFD by polyvinyl fluoride. As a forming process, the reference process \u201cextrusion, plastic pipes\u201d is used.\n\nCurated planning decision: R133-R152:C149-C151-C190. New revision only; original published version preserved.",
